<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var pref = localStorage.getItem('lw-theme') || 'system';
      var resolved = pref === 'system'
        ? (matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: light)').matches ? 'light' : 'dark')
        : pref;
      var root = document.documentElement;
      root.setAttribute('data-theme', resolved);
      root.setAttribute('data-theme-pref', pref);
      root.style.colorScheme = resolved;
      root.style.background = resolved === 'light' ? '#F8FAFC' : '#0F172A';
    })();
  </script>
  <!--
    pages/edit-profile.html — Account Profile
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Reached from pages/settings.html's "Edit Profile" button. Four
    things live here:
      1. Display name edit.
      2. Change Email — RECONCILED this pass: a teammate session built
         this as part of an in-page modal on pages/settings.html at
         the same time this page was built; kept this page as the
         real destination instead (see pages/settings.html's own
         RECONCILED note) and pulled the operation in from there.
      3. Change Password + "forgot your current password" reset email
         — js/account-security.js, added from OUTSIDE js/auth.js
         (see that file's own header comment for why it's safe).
      4. Delete Account — RECONCILED this pass, same story as Change
         Email above.

    XP REMOVAL (this pass): this page used to also carry a fifth thing
    here, an account-wide Level/XP summary card (js/xp.js) — removed,
    along with its initLevelCard() function in js/edit-profile.js and
    the js/xp.js <script> tag below.

    Change Email and Delete Account both call window.LWAuth (js/auth.js
    PROFILE MANAGEMENT block) — .updateUserEmail() reauthenticates then
    sends a confirmation link (the login email doesn't change until
    it's clicked); .deleteAccount() reauthenticates, then flags the
    account for grace-period deletion and signs the learner out — see
    auth.js's deleteAccount() header comment for the full design (this
    pass replaced its old instant hard-delete). Display name also calls
    window.LWAuth — .updateUsername() — rather than the raw doc/db/setDoc
    handles this page used to reach for directly: those were
    deliberately removed from window.LWAuth (see auth.js's SECURITY
    note) since they let anyone in the browser console write arbitrary
    fields to their own Firestore profile.

    GUARD CONFIRM MODAL: every action that changes account state (name,
    email, password, delete) now goes through window.LWConfirmGuard()
    first — a 10-second-countdown "are you sure?" modal, own copy of
    pages/settings.html's (js/settings-page.js), since the two pages
    don't share one DOM. Delete Account additionally requires typing
    "DELETE" first, same as the teammate session's original design —
    it's the single most destructive action on this page.

    CONNECTS : ← pages/settings.html ("Edit Profile" button)
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  -->
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Edit Profile | LinguaWave</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/style.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/app.css" />

  <script type="module" src="../js/auth.js"></script>
  <script type="module" src="../js/account-security.js"></script>
  <!-- Shared icon system. Plain <script> (not a module) and NOT deferred:
       window.LWIcons must exist before any page script, inline script or
       module body runs. See js/icons.js. -->
  <script src="../js/icons.js"></script>
  <script src="../js/theme.js" defer></script>
  <script>
  window.addEventListener('lwauth-ready', () => {
    LWAuth.requireAuth('../index.html');
  });
  </script>
  <style>
    /* Page-scoped, same pattern as pages/settings.html's own <style>
       block: layout only, every color/spacing value still comes from
       css/style.css's tokens. */
    .profile-card { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-6); flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .profile-card__avatar {
      width: 88px; height: 88px; border-radius: 50%; flex-shrink: 0;
      background: var(--clr-accent-soft); color: var(--clr-accent);
      display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--fs-2xl); font-weight: 700;
    }
    .profile-card__info { flex: 1; min-width: 220px; }
    .profile-card__email { color: var(--clr-text-muted); font-size: var(--fs-sm); margin-top: var(--space-2); }
    .password-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-3); }
    /* Delete Account card heading — same red-as-text token
       .modal__section--danger used on pages/settings.html's old
       in-page modal draft, applied here to a plain .card instead. */
    .danger-title { color: var(--clr-red-text); }

    /* Guard confirm modal (RECONCILED — own copy of
       pages/settings.html's, since the two pages don't share a DOM).
       Reuses existing tokens throughout — only the overlay/panel
       shell has no existing equivalent. */
    .modal-overlay {
      position: fixed; inset: 0;
      /* Deliberately NOT --backdrop — that token is a light, blurred
         frosted-glass tint for the sticky .navbar, not a scrim for
         dimming page content behind a modal. Works the same
         regardless of which theme is active. */
      background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.55);
      display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      padding: var(--space-4);
      z-index: 1000; /* same top-layer treatment as .skip-link */
    }
    .modal-overlay[hidden] { display: none; }
    .modal {
      background: var(--clr-surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--clr-border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-xl); /* matches .card */
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
      max-width: 480px; width: 100%; max-height: 90vh; overflow-y: auto;
      padding: var(--space-6);
    }
    .modal:focus { outline: none; }
    .modal__head { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
    .modal--guard { max-width: 400px; }
    .modal--guard p { font-size: var(--fs-sm); color: var(--clr-text); margin: 0 0 var(--space-5); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .modal__actions { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; gap: var(--space-3); }
    /* Keeps the Confirm button's width stable as its label counts down
       from "Confirm (10)" to "Confirm" so it doesn't jump around. */
    .modal__actions .btn--danger { min-width: 8.5em; }
