<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <!-- Same theme-flash-prevention snippet every page in this repo uses.
       Must stay first in <head>. -->
  <script>
    (function () {
      var pref = localStorage.getItem('lw-theme') || 'system';
      var resolved = pref === 'system'
        ? (matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: light)').matches ? 'light' : 'dark')
        : pref;
      var root = document.documentElement;
      root.setAttribute('data-theme', resolved);
      root.setAttribute('data-theme-pref', pref);
      root.style.colorScheme = resolved;
      root.style.background = resolved === 'light' ? '#F8FAFC' : '#0F172A';
    })();
  </script>
  <!--
    pages/mastery-quiz.html — Mastery Quiz (NEW)
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    PURPOSE : A real-native Mastery Quiz screen, replacing the
              hand-off to V1's pages/quiz.html — now covering all 12
              chapters (see SCOPE below). Reuses the SAME mission.items
              QUIZ concept js/missions.js already builds (unchanged
              shape); this page just walks it as its own dedicated
              screen instead of leaving the Mastery Quiz on the
              untouched V1 engine.

    SCOPE (widened this revision — merged from three parallel
              widenings) : gated in js/mastery-quiz.js, now covering
              ALL 12 chapters — Chapter 1 (ASL Foundations), Chapter 2
              (Introduce Yourself), Chapter 3 (Express How You Feel),
              Chapter 4 (Daily Actions & Communication), Chapter 5
              (Describing People & Things), Chapter 6 (Home & Family),
              Chapter 7 (School Life), Chapter 8 (Food & Nature),
              Chapter 9 (Clothing & Belongings), Chapter 10 (People,
              Places & Time), Chapter 11 (Having a Conversation), and
              Chapter 12 (Putting It All Together) — WIDENED this
              revision from the original Chapters 1-2, merging three
              separate widenings (3-5, 6-8, and 9-12) rather than
              keeping any of them partial. Only Chapters 1-2 have
              hand-curated NEAR_NEIGHBORS/discrimination data in
              js/lesson-loop.js — Chapters 3-12 run on that file's
              existing generic (non-curated) distractor fallback, same
              as every other uncurated chapter's lesson flow already
              does. With every chapter now sampled, the V1
              pages/quiz.html hand-off is currently unreachable from
              any real mission link — it remains only as a defensive
              fallback (stale link, typed URL, or a future new chapter
              not yet added to the gate), same "degrade, don't throw"
              discipline as the rest of Missions — see this file's own js
              for the exact gate and how to widen it further.

    ENTRY   : ?mission=<categoryId> — same param convention every
              other page uses.

    CLOSES TWO STANDING GAPS (see Missions_LinguaWave_Progress_Tracker.md
              §5 open question 7, and AI_MEMORY.md's Lesson-engine
              session note):
                1. Hearts are now spent on quiz SUBMIT, not attempt
                   START (every other chapter's Start Mastery Quiz
                   button, in mission-overview.js/lesson.js,
                   still spends on start — untouched, out of this
                   sample's scope).
                2. Passing now actually calls markItemComplete() on
                   the mission's QUIZ item, so mission %/chapter
                   progress/the Missions Completed stat on
                   progress.html can finally reach 100% for a
                   sampled chapter's mission.

    NOT BUILT HERE : the Optional Camera Check V1's quiz.html has is a
              deliberate, explicit omission — it was never part of the
              original mockup spec for the Quiz screen (flagged as
              V1-only "extra" in LinguaWave_Mockup_Visual_Audit.md
              §8) and this build keeps's Mastery Quiz MC-only.
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  -->
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
  <title>Mastery Quiz | LinguaWave</title>

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/style.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/learn.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/app.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/tour.css" />
  <!-- Role guard: admin -> admin pages only, learners -> out of admin pages. Keep synchronous, in <head>. -->
  <script src="../js/role-guard.js"></script>
</head>
<body data-tour="mastery-quiz">

  <a href="#mq-main" class="skip-link">Skip to Mastery Quiz</a>

  <div class="app-shell">
    <aside class="app-sidebar">
      <a href="dashboard.html" class="app-sidebar__logo">Lingua<span>Wave</span></a>
      <nav class="app-sidebar__nav">
        <a href="dashboard.html" class="app-sidebar__link">
          <span class="app-sidebar__icon" aria-hidden="true" data-lw-icon="dashboard"></span>
          Dashboard
        </a>
        <a href="learn.html" class="app-sidebar__link active">
          <span class="app-sidebar__icon" aria-hidden="true" data-lw-icon="learn"></span>
          Learn
        </a>
        <a href="progress.html" class="app-sidebar__link">
          <span class="app-sidebar__icon" aria-hidden="true" data-lw-icon="progress"></span>
          Progress
        </a>
        <a href="game.html" class="app-sidebar__link">
          <span class="app-sidebar__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="4" width="8" height="5" rx="1"/><rect x="13" y="4" width="8" height="5" rx="1"/><rect x="3" y="11" width="5" height="5" rx="1"/><rect x="10" y="11" width="8" height="5" rx="1"/><path d="M4 20h16"/></svg></span>
          Game
        </a>
        <a href="feedback.html" class="app-sidebar__link">
          <span class="app-sidebar__icon" aria-hidden="true" data-lw-icon="feedback"></span>
          Feedback
        </a>
        <a href="settings.html" class="app-sidebar__link">
          <span class="app-sidebar__icon" aria-hidden="true" data-lw-icon="settings"></span>
          Settings
        </a>
      </nav>
      <div class="app-sidebar__foot">
        <button class="theme-switch" id="theme-toggle" type="button" role="switch"
                aria-checked="false" title="Switch to dark theme" aria-label="Switch to dark theme">
          <span class="theme-switch__check">
            <span data-lw-icon="theme_sun" data-lw-icon-self="1" data-lw-icon-class="theme-switch__icon theme-switch__icon--sun"></span>
            <span data-lw-icon="theme_moon" data-lw-icon-self="1" data-lw-icon-class="theme-switch__icon theme-switch__icon--moon"></span>
          </span>
        </button>
        <a href="#" class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" data-logout="../index.html">Log out</a>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <div class="app-main" id="mq-main">

      <section class="section section--sm section--tight">
        <div class="container container--narrow">
          <!-- Back link. This static "All missions" is only what the
               not-found screen keeps (no mission to go back to).
               js/mastery-quiz.js's configureBackLink() repoints it, once
               the mission is known, at the lesson recap slide (when the
               learner arrived with &from=lesson) or the mission's own
               Mission Overview, instead of the whole missions list. -->
          <a href="learn.html" class="back-link" id="mq-back">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 12H5M12 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg>
            <span id="mq-back-label">All missions</span>
          </a>
          <div id="mq-content">
            <!-- filled by js/mastery-quiz.js -->
            <p class="text-muted">Loading quiz…</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>

  <script type="module" src="../js/auth.js"></script>
  <script defer src="../js/data.js"></script>
  <script defer src="../js/missions.js"></script>
  <script src="../js/lesson-loop.js"></script>
  <!-- Shared icon system. Plain <script> (not a module) and NOT deferred:
       window.LWIcons must exist before any page script, inline script or
       module body runs, and before DOMContentLoaded hydrates any
       data-lw-icon="" markup below. See js/icons.js. -->
  <script src="../js/icons.js"></script>
  <script src="../js/theme.js" defer></script>
  <!-- ADDED (migration-analysis pass) — provides window.LinguaWave.showToast
       and, critically, wires up every [data-logout] button (the sidebar's
       Log out link had no handler at all before this, on ANY page). -->
  <script src="../js/main.js"></script>
  <script src="../js/mastery-quiz.js"></script>
  <!-- Guided tour (NEW): what it says lives in js/tour-guides.js, how it runs in
       js/tour.js, how it looks in css/tour.css. This page opts in via
       <body data-tour="mastery-quiz">. -->
  <script src="../js/tour-guides.js"></script>
  <script src="../js/tour.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
