<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <!-- NEW: sets data-theme before any CSS loads, so the page never
       flashes the wrong theme on load. Must stay first in <head>. -->
  <script>
    (function () {
      var pref = localStorage.getItem('lw-theme') || 'system';
      var resolved = pref === 'system'
        ? (matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: light)').matches ? 'light' : 'dark')
        : pref;
      var root = document.documentElement;
      root.setAttribute('data-theme', resolved);
      root.setAttribute('data-theme-pref', pref);
      root.style.colorScheme = resolved;
      // Paints the correct background INSTANTLY, without waiting on
      // css/style.css to finish loading/parsing — this is the part
      // that actually stops the white flash on reload/navigation.
      root.style.background = resolved === 'light' ? '#F8FAFC' : '#0F172A';
    })();
  </script>
  <!--
    pages/homepage.html — Authenticated Homepage / Welcome
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    REV 2 (this session) — redesigned to a marketing-landing-page shape
    (hero → stats → topic grid → ASL info) per reference screenshots of
    Cisco Networking Academy's homepage. Was a single reading page (just
    the old Unit 0 content as static prose) — that content is KEPT, just
    demoted below the new hero/stats/topic-grid sections instead of
    being the whole page. Still answers ONE question overall: "What is
    ASL / welcome to LinguaWave?" — deliberately NOT the Dashboard
    ("what should I do next?") and NOT the Learn trail ("where can I
    go?"). No real usage stats exist for a capstone project, so the
    stats bar below uses REAL content counts pulled from js/data.js at
    build time (unit/sign counts), not invented adoption numbers.

    NEW (this session) — the navbar's user block (greeting name) is now
    a link to pages/dashboard.html, matching the reference's "click
    your profile → go to your dashboard" behavior. Every other
    authenticated page's navbar is UNCHANGED (still just a plain
    <span>) — this was scoped to Homepage only, per the request; ask if
    you want the same link added to dashboard.html/learn.html/
    lesson.html/intro-to-asl.html's navbars too.

    STILL STATIC: no homepage.js. Nothing here is progress-gated or
    learner-specific beyond the name/profile-link in the navbar (filled
    by the same js/main.js every other authenticated page already
    loads). The stats/topic-grid below are hand-written static numbers/
    links, not a live query against js/data.js — see this file's own
    "Subject Areas"-equivalent comment further down for why.

    AUTH     : requireAuth() at the top kicks anyone who isn't logged
               in back to index.html — same guard, same pattern, as
               pages/dashboard.html / pages/learn.html /
               pages/camera-practice.html / pages/intro-to-asl.html.
               ⚠️ js/auth.js is explicitly out of scope — not opened,
               not touched, per every other session's rule.

    CONNECTS : ← index.html            (after login/register, and for
                                          an already-logged-in visitor)
               → pages/dashboard.html  (Dashboard CTA + navbar profile)
               → pages/learn.html      (Start Learning CTA + every
                                          topic-grid card — each opens
                                          straight into that unit)
               → pages/intro-to-asl.html (optional "read more" banner)
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  -->
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Welcome | LinguaWave</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/style.css" />
  <!-- Reuses css/learn.css's .unit-info/.unit-info__section (originally
       built for learn.js's now-removed Unit 0 screen, repurposed) and
       .lesson-card--intro/.category-card__icon for the "Want more?"
       banner further down. No new shared CSS file for this page's own
       hero/stats/topic-grid — only the page-scoped rules below, same
       "small scoped <style> block" pattern pages/intro-to-asl.html
       already uses for its own `.lesson-article` rules. -->
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/learn.css" />

  <script type="module" src="../js/auth.js"></script>
  <!-- Shared icon system. Plain <script> (not a module) and NOT deferred:
       window.LWIcons must exist before any page script, inline script or
       module body runs, and before DOMContentLoaded hydrates any
       data-lw-icon="" markup below. See js/icons.js. -->
  <script src="../js/icons.js"></script>
  <script src="../js/theme.js" defer></script>
  <script>
  window.addEventListener('lwauth-ready', () => {
    LWAuth.requireAuth('../index.html');
  });
  </script>
  <style>
    /* Page-scoped hero/stats/topic-grid layout only — everything else
       reuses css/style.css (.section/.container/.card/.btn/...) and
       css/learn.css (.unit-info/.lesson-card--intro/...) as-is. */

    /* DESIGN PASS (this session) — hero-zone / quote-zone: full-bleed
       background washes (not boxed cards) so the hero and quote read
       as distinct "zones" instead of every section sitting on the same
       flat background at the same visual weight. Same accent-soft
       gradient technique css/dashboard.css's `.continue-card` already
       uses for its own "most important thing on the page" card —
       applied here to a whole section instead of a card. */
    .hero-zone {
      background: radial-gradient(1100px 480px at 15% -20%, var(--clr-accent-soft), transparent 65%);
    }
    .quote-zone {
      background: var(--clr-surface);
      border-block: 1px solid var(--clr-border);
    }

    /* Icon badges — inline SVG (currentColor) in the same rounded
       circle/square "chip" treatment css/learn.css's
       `.category-card__icon` and css/dashboard.css's
       `.continue-card__icon` already use elsewhere in the app, instead
       of a bare emoji glyph. SVG paints identically on every system/
       browser; nothing here depends on a font's emoji fallback. */
    .icon-badge {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      flex: 0 0 auto; color: var(--clr-accent);
    }
    .icon-badge svg { width: 55%; height: 55%; }

    .hero-banner {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-2);
      padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4); border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
