| 09-15 (Backfilled — never logged at the time) — sequential sign gating + sidebar progress-store unification | Two fixes, done together, logged now retroactively since this row was missing. **(1) Sequential sign gating.** Added a real LOCKED/PENDING split so a learner can't reach a sign out of order just because it has a `<a href>` somewhere: LOCKED = the whole mission is chapter-gated (`isChapterUnlocked()`); PENDING = the mission itself is open but an earlier sign in ITS OWN order hasn't been learned yet. `mission-overview.js` gained `isSignAccessible(mission, signs, id)`; the chip loop now renders a non-navigable `<span class="sign-chip--locked">`/`<span class="sign-chip--pending">` (dashed border, still hoverable, no `href`, not focusable) instead of an `<a>` for either state — `css/app.css` got the matching `.sign-chip--pending` rule alongside the existing `--locked` one. `camera-practice.js` mirrors the identical check call-for-call against the SAME mission-item order (`missionSignOrder()`/`isSignAccessible()`, new) so the two pages can't disagree about what's reachable: `boot()` now redirects to Mission Overview (with a toast) if the requested `?sign=` is locked OR pending, and `sidebarSignRow()`/`sidebarCategoryBlock()` render the matching 🔒 non-navigable rows in the course sidebar — same two-state split, `css/lesson.css` got the matching rule. **(2) Sidebar progress-store unification.** The course sidebar's ✔/○ marks and each unit's "X%" badge previously read `window.LWProgress` (the older, separate "practiced via camera" store) while Mission Overview reads `window.LWMissions` (real LESSON/BOOSTER/PRACTICE/QUIZ item completion) — same category could show two disagreeing numbers (e.g. sidebar "86%" vs. Mission Overview "24% complete"). Sidebar now computes both from `window.LWMissions` exclusively (`isItemComplete()`-based), matching Mission Overview's own `getMissionProgress()` fraction exactly for a single-category unit. Not retroactive — old `LWProgress`-only history that never completed a real Mission LESSON item now correctly shows not-done, since the two stores were always tracking different things. **Flagged, not fixed this session:** `camera-practice.html`'s Prev/Next used `window.LWData`'s own sign ordering (separate from the Mission's own order used for the new gating check) — if the two orderings ever drift for a category, Next could land on a sign the pending-check treats as unreached and bounce back to Mission Overview; pre-existing data-parity gap between the two content sources, not introduced by this fix. (This is the same class of gap the 09-15 later-session row below ends up fixing directly for the Next/Prev buttons.) | `js/mission-overview.js`, `js/camera-practice.js`, `css/app.css`, `css/lesson.css`, `AI_MEMORY.md` |
| 09-15 (Quick Check progress-write race, pure Prev/Next navigation, Next Sign → Continue Mission fallback, and the camera-practice link sign param) | Four related fixes to the camera-practice/lesson hand-off, done incrementally across the same conversation as one connected thread. **(1) Quick Check no longer writes progress.** Its correct-answer handler used to call `recordSignPracticed()`/`markSignPracticedBridge()` directly, racing against the SAME call in `setupNavButtons()`'s Prev/Next/Finish — so a correct answer could advance mission progress before the visible page (sidebar checkmarks, mission %) caught up. Removed that write entirely; `markCurrentSignPracticed()` was promoted from a closure private to `setupNavButtons()` to module scope so it has exactly one caller-set now. **(2) Sidebar-exit gap fixed at its real source, not patched via Quick Check.** New `wireSidebarProgressCapture(el)`, wired once off `#course-sidebar` (idempotent via a `dataset` flag — the container itself is never replaced, only re-rendered), delegates on every sidebar `<a>` click and calls the same `markCurrentSignPracticed()` before the browser follows the link — this is what the old Quick-Check-handler write was actually trying to cover. **(3) Prev/Next are now pure navigation.** Both buttons stopped calling `markCurrentSignPracticed()` on click at all — clicking through no longer inflates "practiced" progress with zero real engagement; the only remaining writers are the Practice Check camera round (`quizSigns.forEach()`, unchanged) and "Finish → Category Assessment" (kept, since leaving for the graded quiz is a real milestone, not just paging). **(4) "Next Sign →" → "↻ Continue Mission" fallback, in two passes because item 3 opened a second gap.** First pass: `signOrder` (this page's own `window.LWData.getCategorySigns()` list) and `missionSignOrder(mission)` (`missions.js`'s independently-forked list — see the still-open data-parity gap flagged in the row above) can disagree in LENGTH, not just gating — e.g. data.js's `people` category has 14 signs (…Boy/Girl/Baby) while missions.js's copy only tracks 11 (…Student). Before this fix, clicking Next past Student walked a learner straight into orphaned content the mission has no LESSON item for at all, so Next started checking whether `signOrder[signIdx+1]` is in `missionSignOrder(mission)`; if not, the button becomes `↻ Continue Mission` and routes to `lesson.html?mission=<category>`, which resumes at `getDropOffIndex(mission)` — the learner's real next incomplete step, not a restart. That first pass only caught the not-tracked case, though — it didn't check whether a *tracked* next sign was actually reachable yet. Because item (3) above stopped Prev/Next from auto-marking a sign learned, a learner who just pages Next/Next/Next never completes a `LESSON` item, so the very next sign can flip PENDING (per `isSignAccessible()`, the same sequential gate `boot()` already enforces, from the earlier sequential-gating session) on the very next click — and until the second pass, clicking `Next Sign →` in that state silently fell through to `boot()`'s own guard, which bounced the learner to Mission Overview with a toast: confusing, since the button they clicked said "Next." `nextAvailable` now checks two conditions instead of one: not-tracked (the original case) OR pending-per-`isSignAccessible()` (the second-pass addition). Either one flips the button to `↻ Continue Mission` before the doomed navigation ever fires. `← Previous` is unaffected by this check (only forward movement can walk off the mission's tracked end or into a not-yet-learned sign). **(5) `cameraPracticeLinkHtml()` missing `sign=` param, found while working the same flow.** `cameraPracticeLinkHtml(mission, signId)`'s one call site (`renderLessonWatch`) already had the specific sign available (`item.signId`), but the function itself never accepted or appended a `sign=` param at all — every "Practice with your camera" link built from a lesson step landed on `camera-practice.html`'s first sign in the category, regardless of which sign the learner was actually on. Confirmed via a concrete case: from "Girl" (item 9 of 40 in `personal_information`), the link should read `camera-practice.html?level=medium&category=personal_information&sign=GIRL` but previously dropped the `sign=` segment entirely. Fixed: `cameraPracticeLinkHtml()` now takes the `signId` parameter and appends `&sign=<signId>` to the built URL when one is passed; the one call site now passes `item.signId` through. Single call site, so no fan-out risk. Verified: `node --check` clean after each edit, no jsdom/browser pass (same standing project limitation as every prior session). **Not done, flagged:** the sidebar link click capture (item 2) still writes progress for ANY sidebar navigation, including to an adjacent sign — inconsistent with Prev/Next now being pure nav; raised to the user, not yet resolved either way. The underlying `data.js`-vs-`missions.js` sign-list mismatch itself (root cause of item 4's first pass) is still open — only worked around at the Next-button level, not fixed at the source. | `js/camera-practice.js`, `js/lesson.js`, `AI_MEMORY.md` |
